<title>UK: Swedbank Japan yen debt rating raised.</title>
<headline>Swedbank Japan yen debt rating raised.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedbank said on Friday its rating for yen-denominated bond issues in Japan has been raised to AA minus from A plus by the Japanese rating institution Nippon Investors Service (NIS).</p>
<p>The decision followed the annual review of Swedbank by NIS in September, Swedbank said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;NIS points out that the bank has now left behind the financial crisis of the early 1990's and that its earnings have improved remarkably since 1993,&quot; Swedbank said. Problem loans have diminished and the quality of its assets continues to improve, according to NIS, Swedbank said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 6176</p>
